{"candidates":[{"file":"src/session/infrastructure/persistence/relational/repositories/session.repository.ts","symbol":"SessionRelationalRepository.deleteByUserIdWithExclude","start_line":99,"end_line":109,"explanation":"The exclusion filter is `id: Not(Number(conditions.userId))`. It compares the session id with the user id instead of `conditions.excludeSessionId`. So the current session is not protected and is soft-deleted, and its next refresh returns 401. A different session whose id happens to equal the user id is the one that survives. That matches the 'unrelated older session sometimes survives' symptom."},{"file":"src/session/infrastructure/persistence/document/repositories/session.repository.ts","symbol":"SessionDocumentRepository.deleteByUserIdWithExclude","start_line":82,"end_line":93,"explanation":"This is the Mongo counterpart. Its body is truncated in the snippet, so I couldn't check it. It could make the same mistake of excluding by userId instead of excludeSessionId in the `_id: { $not: ... }` filter. This is a secondary suspect."}],"fix":{"file":"src/session/infrastructure/persistence/relational/repositories/session.repository.ts","description":"In deleteByUserIdWithExclude, change the exclusion to use the session id: `id: Not(Number(conditions.excludeSessionId))`. Keep the `user: { id: Number(conditions.userId) }` filter. Check that the document repository excludes `conditions.excludeSessionId` as well.","replacement_code":"await this.sessionRepository.softDelete({
  user: { id: Number(conditions.userId) },
  id: Not(Number(conditions.excludeSessionId)),
});"}}

fix.replacement_code:
